  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#the-datatransferitemlist-interface\n\nThe DataTransferItemList interface defines the following WebIDL methods:\n\n``` idl\n  DataTransferItem? add(DOMString data, DOMString type);\n  DataTransferItem? add(File data);\n```\n\nAnd defines the behavior of these methods based on the type of the first argument to the method:\n\n> ↪ If the first argument to the method is a string\n> ↪ If the first argument to the method is a File\n\nIt should be clarified as to what the correct behavior is if the first parameter passed to the function is a File, and the second is a DOMString. Should the File steps be taken and the second parameter ignored, or should the DOMString steps be taken, and the File coerced into a DOMString?\n\nChrome appears to take the second path, as does Firefox's current implementation in Aurora.\n",
